# Trivy ignore file — spc-bot image.
#
# Policy (enforced by the docker-publish Trivy gate): the release is blocked
# when the image contains a NEW FIXABLE CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerability. The gate
# runs:
#   trivy image --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH
#               --ignore-unfixed --exit-code 1
#
# NOTE: the gate is deliberately vuln-only. A secret scanner was tried on the
# gate and produced an unreproducible finding that blocked a legitimate
# release with no triage path (verified 2026-08-15). Secret scanning remains
# available as a manual/CI check; it must not hard-block releases until it has
# a documented suppression mechanism and a burn-in period.
#
# --ignore-unfixed already excludes every CVE with NO published fix, so
# no-fix CVEs (media codecs, transitive geo-stack deps, pending-Debian core
# libs) never reach the gate and are NOT listed here. Do NOT add no-fix CVEs
# to this file: the moment Debian publishes a fix, --ignore-unfixed stops
# suppressing them and this file must not silently swallow them instead.
#
# This file lists ONLY fixable CVEs that are accepted risk with evidence:

# Build-layer ghosts (verified 2026-08-14): these packages exist only in the
# wheel COPY layer of the image history, not in the final runtime filesystem
# (pip show / import both fail in the built image). The wheels dir is rm'd at
# runtime; only the layer history carries the vulnerable files. They are
# fixable, so --ignore-unfixed does NOT exclude them — hence the entries.
CVE-2025-47273
# setuptools 70.3.0 wheel in COPY layer; not importable in final image.
# Builder pins setuptools>=78.1.1; remove this entry after a clean rebuild
# confirms the wheel layer no longer carries 70.3.0 (check: trivy image
# without --ignorefile shows no setuptools finding). Re-check by 2026-09-01.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
# msgpack 1.1.2 wheel in COPY layer; not importable in final image.
# Transitive via sounderpy build; remove this entry after a clean rebuild
# confirms the wheel layer no longer carries 1.1.2. Re-check by 2026-09-01.
